        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The most frustrating issue with generic newline removers is that they destroy paragraph structure, concatenating hundreds of distinct thoughts into an unreadable monolithic block. FastToolVerse provides an intelligent <strong>Preserve paragraph breaks</strong> option that separates text into distinct semantic blocks:
        </p>
        
        <div class="not-prose my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 overflow-x-auto space-y-2">
          <div><span class="text-slate-500">// Intelligent paragraph preservation logic</span></div>
          <div>const paragraphs = text.split(/(?:\r?\n\s*){'{2,}'}/);</div>
          <div>const result = paragraphs.map(p =&gt; &#123;</div>
          <div class="pl-4">return p.split(/\r?\n/)</div>
          <div class="pl-8">.map(line =&gt; line.trim())</div>
          <div class="pl-8">.filter(line =&gt; line.length &gt; 0)</div>
          <div class="pl-8">.join(' ');</div>
          <div>&#125;).join('\n\n');</div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          By splitting across double line returns (<code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">\n\n</code>), internal sentence fragments are cleanly stitched together while paragraph boundaries remain intact.
