        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Removing line breaks is a critical formatting requirement across multiple computing workflows:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Fixing PDF Reflow:</strong> Copying text from multi-column research papers or PDF eBooks frequently embeds a hard newline at the end of every line. Replacing breaks with a single space restores fluent reading prose.</li>
          <li><strong>SQL <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">WHERE id IN (...)</code> Formatting:</strong> Database administrators often copy vertical columns of primary keys from spreadsheets. Joining lines with commas instantly formats the list for SQL clauses.</li>
          <li><strong>JSON and YAML String Sanitization:</strong> Multiline strings copied into JSON attributes cause syntax errors unless newlines are collapsed or escaped. FastToolVerse flattens strings in one click.</li>
          <li><strong>Social Media &amp; Meta Descriptions:</strong> Flattening copy ensures character counters accurately reflect single-line character lengths for SEO title tags and meta descriptions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section (SEO crawlable) -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
